          "title": "Toward Interactive Understanding of Code APIs",
          "title_zh": "迈向代码 API 的交互式理解",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.32081v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.32081",
          "summary": "The paper introduces PAU, a benchmark that gives models only black-box, API-level access to Python snippets, so they must probe the code with exploratory inputs and infer its functionality, framing this as unsupervised tool understanding. Frontier models struggle, with Claude-4-Opus failing to understand over 45% of the test set, and the authors trace this to overconfidence and insufficient exploration; post-training with an Asymmetric Actor Critic approach lets an AAC-tuned Qwen3-8B match GPT-5-mini.",
