          "title": "GameBoyWorlds: A Testbed for Self-Improvement in Embodied Video Games",
          "title_zh": "GameBoyWorlds：具身电子游戏自我改进的测试平台",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.32093v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.32093",
          "summary": "GameBoyWorlds is a testbed for agentic self-improvement in video games: its Execution split spans 5 game series and 500 tasks where agents get training games but no demonstrations, documentation, or rewards, while its Playthrough split tests end-to-end completion of two fan-made Pokémon games. Out-of-the-box frontier models complete fewer than 50% of the execution tasks, and the authors show that world modelling and autonomous skill discovery fail while a curiosity-driven guide-writing strategy achieves only partial success; a sophisticated agentic pipeline with multimodal memory and hierarchical subgoals fails to reach the first major milestone in either playthrough.",
