          "title": "Graph Forward Distribution Matching for Molecular Inverse Design",
          "title_zh": "用于分子逆向设计的图前向分布匹配",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2609.32056v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2609.32056",
          "summary": "GraphFDM is an online reinforcement learning paradigm for graph diffusion that optimizes through the forward process, using valid generations to define a reward-tilted target distribution jointly over graph size and molecular structure for each property condition without storing reverse trajectories. In multi-conditional polymer and small-molecule generation it reports the lowest MAE on every target property, with reductions of up to 53.0% relative to the strongest baselines and chemical validity above 0.99.",
